# ============================================================
# HYG-1: line-ending and encoding normalisation.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#   Without it, a Windows editor rewrote 18 tracked files from LF to CRLF,
#   producing an 8,600-line phantom diff in which only ~113 lines were real
#   change. That is not cosmetic:
#     * code review becomes impossible — real edits hide inside the noise;
#     * commit 9339835 ("Use pending status for staged sync runs", 15 real
#       lines) silently carried a full-file re-encode that turned every em dash
#       in worker/index.mjs into mojibake, which then needed commit 1081ae4 to
#       undo;
#     * every concurrent branch conflicts on every line of every file.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` stores text as LF in the repository regardless of the
# platform that wrote it, so this class of diff cannot recur.
# ============================================================

* text=auto eol=lf

# ---- Explicit text types (belt and braces) ---------------------------------
*.ts    text eol=lf
*.tsx   text eol=lf
*.js    text eol=lf
*.mjs   text eol=lf
*.cjs   text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.css   text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.sql   text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.txt   text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf

# ---- Binary: never diffed, never line-ending converted ---------------------
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pyc   binary

# ---- Generated: collapse in reviews, still tracked where relevant ----------
package-lock.json linguist-generated=true -diff
pnpm-lock.yaml    linguist-generated=true -diff
